compliance) sit in Appendix 1, a separate document.","fy":"2025/26","as_of_doc":"TREASURY MANAGEMENT OUTTURN REPORT 2025/26","as_of_url":"https://www.minutes.haringey.gov.uk/documents/s158540/02. Cover Report Treasury Management Outturn 2025.26.pdf","as_of_date":"2026-07-23","signals":[{"code":"borrowing-increase","headline":"Loans up \u00a3232.1m in 2025/26 to \u00a31,213.4m at 31 March 2026, with the capital programme to be financed largely by new borrowing in upcoming years","why":"A 24% one-year jump in debt, with more signalled, raises debt-servicing costs just as short-term LA-to-LA rates spiked to 5-7% at year end."},{"code":"low-liquidity","headline":"Investment balances fell as low as \u00a313.6m during 2025/26 (range \u00a313.6m-\u00a3184.3m) against a \u00a31.2bn loan book, with portfolio weighted average maturity of 1 day","why":"A council of this debt size running an overnight-only cash book with a \u00a313.6m trough depends on continuous access to short-term borrowing markets."}],"key_figures":[{"name":"borrowing","value":"\u00a31,213.4m loans, an increase of \u00a3232.1m compared to 31 March 2025 (\u00a31,141.9m at 31 December 2025)","as_at":"31/3/26","page":3},{"name":"investments","value":"balances ranged \u00a313.6m-\u00a3184.3m during 2025/26; year-end rate of return 3.75%, weighted average maturity 1 day, credit rating AA-","as_at":"31/3/26","page":4},{"name":"compliance exception","value":"full compliance except lease levels vs the Operational Boundary and Authorised Limit (detailed in Appendix 1 section 8; also reported at Q3)","as_at":"2025/26","page":4}],"commercial":null,"tms_components":null},"compliance":null,"documents":[{"title":"Background paper 1 - Corona Energy Retail 4 Limited Annual Report and Financial Statements for the year ended 31 March 2025","url":"http://www.minutes.haringey.gov.uk/documents/s158808/background-paper-1-corona-energy-retail-4-limited-annual-rep.pdf","committee":"Cabinet Member Signing","date":"12/08/2026","key"