status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://www.minutes.haringey.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-13","committee":"Housing, Planning and Development Scrutiny Panel","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://www.minutes.haringey.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-13","committee":"Culture, Community Safety & Environment Scrutiny Panel","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://www.minutes.haringey.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-15","committee":"Pensions Committee and Board","time":"7.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://www.minutes.haringey.gov.uk"}],"recent":[{"date":"2026-08-07","committee":"Cabinet Member Signing","time":"3.30 pm","status":"Confirmed; The acquisition of 21 newly constructed homes located at 76 Mayes Road, Wood Green N22 6SY","webcast":false,"url":"https://www.minutes.haringey.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-08-10","committee":"Cabinet Member Signing","time":"11.30 am","status":"Confirmed; Correction of a Company Name for Award of Two Concession Contracts to Operate and Expand Dockless Bike Services in Haringey over the next four years","webcast":false,"url":"https://www.minutes.haringey.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-08-10","committee":"Cabinet Member Signing","time":"2.00 pm","status":"Confirmed; Major Works Programme Broadwater Farm Estate","webcast":false,"url":"https://www.minutes.haringey.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-08-12","committee":"Cabinet Member Signing","time":"1.00 pm","status":"Confirmed; Gas Contract - Cabinet Correction Report","webcast":false,"url":"https://www.minutes.haringey.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-15","committee":"Cabinet","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://www.minutes.haringey.gov.uk"}]},"news":[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"External borrowing increased 23.6% in one year; HRA borrowing up 17.6%","lead":"A 23.6% year-on-year increase in borrowing raises sustainability questions. When a council describes its own borrowing trajectory as 'not sustainable', it signals expected financial pressure ahead.","iso":"2026-07-23","paper_title":"Appendix1_TreasuryManagementOutturnReport-2025-26 V1 , item 11.","paper_url":"https://www.minutes.haringey.gov.uk/documents/s158541/Appendix1_TreasuryManagementOutturnReport-2025-26 V1.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"PFI and finance lease liabilities breach authorised prudential limit","lead":"Exceeding prudential limits in a specific borrowing category reduces headroom and shows the council is operating outside its approved strategy. Persistent breaches may signal deteriorating financial discipline.","iso":"2026-07-23","paper_title":"Appendix1_TreasuryManagementOutturnReport-2025-26 V1 , item 11.","paper_url":"https://www.minutes.haringey.gov.uk/documents/s158541/Appendix1_TreasuryManagementOutturnReport-2025-26 V1.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"\u00a350m LOBO loans face refinancing demand within 12 months at materially higher rates","lead":"This is an immediate refinancing obligation. If lenders call, the council faces significantly higher borrowing costs when refinancing at current rates, increasing annual debt service.","iso":"2026-07-23","paper_title":"Appendix1_TreasuryManagementOutturnReport-2025-26 V1 , item 11.","paper_url":"https://www.minutes.haringey.gov.uk/documents/s158541/Appendix1_TreasuryManagementOutturnReport-2025-26 V1.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-07-23","committee":"Audit Committee","paper_title":"Appendix1_TreasuryManagementOutturnReport-2025-26 V1 , item 11.","paper_url":"https://www.minutes.haringey.gov.uk/documents/s158541/Appendix1_TreasuryManagementOutturnReport-2025-26 V1.pdf","headline":"External borrowing increased 23.6% in one year; HRA borrowing up 17.6%","detail":"Total external borrowing rose from \u00a3981.3m to \u00a31,213.4m (\u00a3232.1m increase). The underlying Capital Financing Requirement increased from \u00a31,418.9m to \u00a31,565.0m. HRA CFR increased particularly sharply from \u00a3626.8m to \u00a3736.9m. This trajectory, combined with high interest rates, underpins the council's assessment that borrowing growth is unsustainable.","category":"borrowing","matters":"A 23.6% year-on-year increase in borrowing raises sustainability questions. When a council describes its own borrowing trajectory as 'not sustainable', it signals expected financial pressure ahead.","figures":"External borrowing: \u00a3981.3m (2024/25) to \u00a31,213.4m (2025/26). CFR: \u00a31,418.9m to \u00a31,565.0m. HRA CFR: \u00a3626.8m to \u00a3736.9m.","quote":"the Council held \u00a31,213.4 million in loans on 31 March 2026, an increase of \u00a3232.1 million compared to 31 March 2025.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-07-23","committee":"Audit Committee","paper_title":"Appendix1_TreasuryManagementOutturnReport-2025-26 V1 , item 11.","paper_url":"https://www.minutes.haringey.gov.uk/documents/s158541/Appendix1_TreasuryManagementOutturnReport-2025-26 V1.pdf","headline":"PFI and finance lease liabilities breach authorised prudential limit","detail":"PFI and finance lease balances reached \u00a345.0m at year-end, breaching the authorised limit of \u00a313.9m by \u00a331.1m and the operational boundary of \u00a312.7m. The council explicitly notes this as an exception to full compliance. This breach was also reported at Q3.","category":"governance","matters":"Exceeding prudential limits in a specific borrowing category reduces headroom and shows the council is operating outside its approved strategy. Persistent breaches may signal deteriorating financial discipline.","figures":"Actual \u00a345.0m; Authorised Limit \u00a313.9m (breach \u00a331.1m); Operational Boundary \u00a312.7m.","quote":"all treasury management activities carried out during the period complied fully with the principles in the Treasury Management Code and the Council's approved Treasury Management Strategy with the exception of lease levels in comparison to the Operational Boundary and Authorised Limit as detailed below, which was also reported in the Quarter 3 monitoring report earlier in the year.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-07-23","committee":"Audit Committee","paper_title":"Appendix1_TreasuryManagementOutturnReport-2025-26 V1 , item 11.","paper_url":"https://www.minutes.haringey.gov.uk/documents/s158541/Appendix1_TreasuryManagementOutturnReport-2025-26 V1.pdf","headline":"\u00a350m LOBO loans face refinancing demand within 12 months at materially higher rates","detail":"All \u00a350m of Haringey's LOBO loans have call dates within April 2026. If lenders exercise these options, the council will need to refinance or repay. Current market rates for 10-year PWLB borrowing (5.72%) are substantially higher than the LOBO loans' current 4.73% rate.","category":"borrowing","matters":"This is an immediate refinancing obligation. If lenders call, the council faces significantly higher borrowing costs when refinancing at current rates, increasing annual debt service.","figures":"\u00a350m LOBO loans at 4.73% weighted average rate. Next call dates: 10/04/2026. Current 10-year PWLB rate: 5.72%.","quote":"All LOBO loans the Council held at year end have call dates within the next 12 months.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-07-23","committee":"Audit Committee","paper_title":"Appendix1_TreasuryManagementOutturnReport-2025-26 V1 , item 11.","paper_url":"https://www.minutes.haringey.gov.uk/documents/s158541/Appendix1_TreasuryManagementOutturnReport-2025-26 V1.pdf","headline":"Council to review and pause capital schemes due to unsustainable borrowing growth","detail":"Haringey will review its capital programme during summer 2026 to identify schemes that can be paused or slowed. The council explicitly cites high interest rates, ongoing reliance on EFS, and unsustainable year-on-year borrowing increases as drivers. This represents a material shift in capital spending plans.","category":"capital","matters":"A council actively pausing capital schemes signals financial distress and indicates a deterioration in financial position. For lenders, this is a leading indicator of financial difficulty and reduced investment capacity.","figures":"External borrowing increased \u00a3232.1m to \u00a31,213.4m in 2025/26. Capital Financing Requirement increased \u00a3146.1m to \u00a31,565.0m.","quote":"the Council will be reviewing its capital programme to identify schemes that can be paused  / slowed down given that interest rates remain high , reliance on EFS remains high and forecast year on year increase on borrowing is not sustainable.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-07-23","committee":"Audit Committee","paper_title":"STATUTORY RECOMMENDATION IN ACCORDANCE WITH SCHEDULE 7 OF THE LOCAL AUDIT AND ACCOUNTABILITY ACT","paper_url":"https://www.minutes.haringey.gov.uk/documents/s158652/Audit Committee Covering Report.pdf","headline":"Council seeks to reduce reliance on Exceptional Financial Support through increased savings delivery","detail":"The statutory officer's finance comments note that acceptance of KPMG's recommendations and council actions is 'expected to increase the level of savings agreed by the Council for 2027/28 onwards, improve delivery of these savings and reduce future reliance on Exceptional Financial Support.' This indicates the council currently depends on emergency government funding to balance its budget.","category":"savings","matters":"Councils reliant on Exceptional Financial Support are in financial distress; reducing that reliance requires closing structural deficits through service cuts or transformation, which poses ongoing financial risk.","figures":"None specific on savings gaps or EFS amounts","quote":"The Statutory Recommendation and Non-Statutory Recommendations and the actions by the Council is expected to increase the level of savings agreed by the Council for 2027/28 onwards, improve delivery of these savings and reduce future reliance on Exceptional Financial Support","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-08-12"},"name":"Haringey","findings_total":87,"news_drafts_total":3}}